---------------
The Chinchilla Scaling Law:

    >   The idea is how do we scale the model
    >   If the parameters are currently 8B and if we increase it to 16B parameters and can we get twice the
        performance from the model?
    >   Number of parameters (Directly Proportional) Number of training token

    But this law has lost it's fame lately because of a lot of inference techniques which are help use to squeeze a lot
    with even less parameters like RAG

